review:
In theory the game could be fun. The graphics are impressive, the guns feel fun to use, the environments and mission ideas themselves are unique, however the major flaw that holds this game back is;

The god awful connection problems
 Every match that I played had frequent freezing and stuttering, as well as a few straight up disconnections, making the game almost unplayable

Ok. This game has the potential for so much, but it feels like it got abandoned after the release of Early Access...
If you haven't tried it yet, wait for more content to be available.
There are literally 3 things to do:
-Glide;
-Build;
-Survey;
That's it. Nothing else.

The general gameplay formula is relaxing and the concept is cool
But the character designs (particularly the nameless humans) are very ugly and unappealing;
Not to mention the game has broken English at time (referring to a single person as they for example), breaking the immersion a fair bit;
The (almost obligatory) upgrades feel overly expensive;
The chiseling gets boring and repetitive real fast, especially with the overuse of the purple (one side ship only) blocks;
If you leave items around your workbench there's a good chance they'll get somewhere that you can't reach cuz nothing position properly;
item upcycling feels super clunky and most times feels like you're attaching parts wrong, which is very unpleasant;
Ordering necessary items is WAY too expensive, making you loose money most times
The market days feel like they should work the other way around, more with the seller choosing what to sell and bargaining the price, instead it works exactly like the normal store with randoms (or at least it feels that way);
If you have items spread around the shop it's allot harder to find what you need since there is no search function and even hovering the items only sometimes works to show you the name;
There should be a way to re-check special order components without needing to summon the buyer again, if there is, it's not clear;

The game has a lot of potential but it's very unrefined in every area, maybe check back in a year, my main issues with it below with just 2.4 hours; 

Controls: it feels like it was meant to be played on a mobile, no amount of tweaking in the settings could fix how bad the controls were
Voices: the voices just piss me off most of the time because they are clearly AI and have little to no emotion to them

Well I had a great time with it, but for a narrative focused experience that also wants you to replay it;

I can never recommend this game. Not until they add a feature to skip cutscenes.

Additionally it would be really handy for your notepad to persist through new games since there's no way to recover it once you complete the game, and there's only one save file.
